**Summary of behavior implemented:**
- `-i` (short, clusterable) and `--ignore-case` (long) are accepted; last occurrence wins (idempotent, always sets to 1).
- Comparison folds only `A`–`Z` → `a`–`z` on both haystack and needle bytes; bytes ≥ 0x80, punctuation, and lowercase are untouched.
- Emitted bytes are never altered; only the matching decision is affected.
- All existing behaviors (prefix, recursion, exit codes, error handling) are preserved unchanged.

